# Keephy Platform - AI Agent Rules

**⚠️ CRITICAL: This file is automatically loaded by Cursor AI. All AI agents MUST follow these rules.**

## Primary Standards Document
**ALWAYS READ FIRST**: `.cursor/rules/CODING_STANDARDS.md`

Before writing ANY code, you MUST:
1. Read `.cursor/rules/CODING_STANDARDS.md` completely
2. Check `.cursor/rules/ARCHITECTURE.md` for architecture patterns
3. Follow all standards and conventions defined in these files

## Quick Reference - Critical Rules

### Code Quality
- ✅ NO syntax errors - Code must compile/run without errors
- ✅ NO mock data in production code - Use real APIs
- ✅ NO hardcoded values - Use configuration/environment variables
- ✅ NO TODO comments - Implement or create proper ticket
- ✅ NO console.log in production - Use structured logging
- ✅ NO commented-out code - Remove it
- ✅ NO minimal versions - Always write enhanced, production-ready versions
- ✅ NO .md files - Do NOT create documentation files unless explicitly asked

### Best Practices & Principles
- ✅ Always use ACID, SOLID, DRY and other best practices
- ✅ Follow industry best practices and design patterns
- ✅ Write production-ready code with full features
- ✅ Always enhanced implementations - Never minimal versions

### AI Agent Expertise Requirements
- ✅ **Backend/API**: Act as 20 years experience world best lead engineer/expert
- ✅ **Frontend UI/UX**: Act as 20 years experience world best lead frontend developer/expert
- ✅ **Attention to details**: Pay very close attention to UI/UX details
- ✅ **Code Review**: Always review code as 20 years experience technical team lead

### Platform Requirements
- ✅ Use `@keephy/i18n` for ALL user-facing text (English, Arabic, Spanish)
- ✅ All frontend pages MUST support SSR (Server-Side Rendering)
- ✅ Use `@keephy/ui-core` for all UI components (NOT shadcn directly)
- ✅ Customize UI components in `packages/ui-core` as per business logic
- ✅ Use Supabase as database
- ✅ Use SendGrid for email service
- ✅ Use original Webflow classes, not Tailwind (where applicable)
- ✅ Use CDN-based assets for CSS/resources

### Architecture
- ✅ Follow ACID principles for database transactions
- ✅ Follow SOLID principles
- ✅ Follow Clean Architecture patterns
- ✅ One service = One domain
- ✅ Use NestJS for backend services
- ✅ Use Next.js with SSR for frontend
- ✅ Use TypeORM for database access

### File Organization
- ✅ Always keep files in proper place - Follow directory structure
- ✅ Components in atomic design folders (atoms, molecules, organisms)
- ✅ Services in feature-specific modules
- ✅ No orphaned files - Every file must have clear purpose

### Code Style
- ✅ 2 spaces indentation
- ✅ Single quotes for strings
- ✅ Always use semicolons
- ✅ Maximum 100 characters per line
- ✅ kebab-case for files, PascalCase for components/classes
- ✅ camelCase for variables/functions

### Before Committing Code
- [ ] Code compiles without errors
- [ ] All tests pass
- [ ] Linting passes
- [ ] No hardcoded values
- [ ] No mock data
- [ ] i18n used for all text
- [ ] SSR supported (frontend)
- [ ] Error handling implemented
- [ ] Input validation added
- [ ] Logging added
- [ ] ACID, SOLID, DRY principles followed
- [ ] Enhanced version (not minimal) implemented
- [ ] Code reviewed as 20 years experience team lead
- [ ] Files in proper locations
- [ ] Using @keephy/ui-core (not shadcn directly)
- [ ] NO .md files created (unless asked)

## File Locations
